    {
      "text": "So I live out in the countryside, and here's the thing. I don't own a car or even a bike. Honestly, I just never learned how to drive. That means every time I have to go somewhere, an appointment, meeting a friend, even just picking up food from the supermarket, I rely completely on the bus. Now, here's the frustrating part. The buses only come once every hour. So if I miss one, I'm stuck waiting, and the next bus feels like it takes forever. That's probably what I dislike the most about living here. It makes something simple like buying groceries feel like a bit of a mission. But on the other hand, there's a side I really love. Most of the time, I get to enjoy complete quietness. There's fresh air, wide open space, and the sound of local birds every morning, and honestly, that makes up for the hassle of catching the bus. Sometimes when I'm standing at the bus stop, a little annoyed, I just remind myself, \"I get to come home to peace, to trees, to nature,\" and I think,\"Yeah,  it's worth it.\"",
      "start_time": 0.079,
      "end_time": 68.959,
